{
  "configuration_id": "config_010",
  "reason": "With only one completed experiment (config_016: multimodal, pca_n2000, resnet50, singleprofile, concat → 52.7% acc), the most fundamental uncertainty is the individual contribution of each modality. Without single-modality baselines, we cannot determine whether the multimodal result is driven primarily by image features, RNA features, or a genuine synergistic effect. config_010 (image_only, singleprofile, resnet50) uses the exact same image encoder and profile setting as the multimodal baseline, making it a clean ablation. If image-only approaches or exceeds 52.7%, RNA is adding little and future effort should focus on image encoder upgrades (e.g., ViT-L). If image-only is substantially lower, RNA is contributing meaningfully and we should prioritize exploring RNA encoders (scvi, scgpt) and fusion strategies. This single experiment maximally reduces uncertainty about the most important design axis before committing budget to more complex multimodal variants."
}

